.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.CLONE" "3JS" "August 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.clone \- LanguageModel: clone() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]clone()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R]
interface creates a copy of the \f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] it is called
on, including its full context window state.
The cloned session can be used independently without affecting the
original.
.PP
The original and the clone share the same context history up to the
point of cloning, enabling you to explore multiple response paths or
test variations without starting from scratch.
.PP
For example, you might build a shared context using \f[CR]append()\f[R]
or early \f[CR]prompt()\f[R] \f[CR]prompt()\f[R] calls, clone the
session, and then send different follow\-up prompts to each clone in
parallel.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
clone()
clone(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object representing the options that can be passed.
If this argument is absent, the \f[CR]options\f[R] from the original
session, such as its abort signal, are used.
Properties include:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]signal\f[R]
An \f[CR]AbortSignal\f[R] to cancel the clone operation.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with a cloned
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] instance.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]AbortError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the operation was canceled via the \f[CR]signal\f[R] option.
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if usage of the method is blocked by a \f[CR]language\-model\f[R]
\f[CR]Permissions\-Policy\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]OperationError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if cloning fails for any other reason not listed in the other
exception types.
.SH EXAMPLES
See also Using the Prompt API > Cloning a session.
.SS Exploring multiple response paths
The following example shows how to explore different response paths.
First, it creates a single session with the start of a story.
Then it clones the original session twice before prompting for different
endings.
This approach preserves the original session in case more exploration is
wanted.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create({
  initialPrompts: [
    { role: \(dqsystem\(dq, content: \(dqYou are a creative writing assistant.\(dq },
  ],
});

\f[B]await\f[R] session.append(
  \(dqThe story begins in a small coastal town during a storm.\(dq,
);

\f[B]const\f[R] [clone1, clone2] = \f[B]await\f[R] Promise.all([session.clone(), session.clone()]);

\f[B]const\f[R] [ending1, ending2] = \f[B]await\f[R] Promise.all([
  clone1.prompt(\(dqWrite a happy ending.\(dq),
  clone2.prompt(\(dqWrite a mysterious ending.\(dq),
]);

console.log(\(dqHappy ending:\(dq, ending1);
console.log(\(dqMysterious ending:\(dq, ending2);
.EE
.SS Cloning to retry after a context overflow
This example uses a checkpoint and rollback pattern to save the state of
a session before attempting to append a large amount of data.
Cloning the session before calling \f[CR]append()\f[R] allows the app to
restore the state if the context window is exceeded.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] veryLargeDocument = \(dqThis is my very long story...\(dq;
\f[B]let\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();
\f[B]const\f[R] checkpoint = \f[B]await\f[R] session.clone();

\f[B]try\f[R] {
  \f[B]await\f[R] session.append(veryLargeDocument);
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (err) {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (err.name === \(dqQuotaExceededError\(dq) {
    console.warn(\(dqDocument too large.\(dq);
    session = checkpoint;
  }
}
.EE
.SS Cloning a session with an abort signal
The following example creates a timeout to abort the clone operation if
it takes more than three seconds.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] controller = \f[B]new\f[R] AbortController();
setTimeout(() \f[B]=>\f[R] controller.abort(), 3000);

\f[B]try\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] clonedSession = \f[B]await\f[R] session.clone({
    signal: controller.signal,
  });
  console.log(\(dqSession cloned successfully.\(dq);
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (err) {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (err.name === \(dqAbortError\(dq) {
    console.log(\(dqClone operation was aborted.\(dq);
  }
}
.EE
